<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Relative frequency and expected frequency</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(cx=0)"]]Wanjiru tosses a soda bottle top \({@N@}\) times. It lands printed side up \({@k@}\) times.[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]Ouma drops a drawing pin \({@N@}\) times. It lands point up \({@k@}\) times.[[elif test="is(cx=2)"]]An agro-dealer in Eldoret tests \({@N@}\) maize seeds from an old batch. \({@k@}\) of them germinate.[[else]]At a junction in [[if test="is(ix=4)"]]Nakuru[[else]]Thika[[/if]], \({@N@}\) boda boda riders are observed. \({@k@}\) of them wear a helmet.[[/if]]</p><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) Find the relative frequency with which [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]the bottle top lands printed side up[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]the pin lands point up[[elif test="is(cx=2)"]]a seed germinates[[else]]a rider wears a helmet[[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Estimate the probability that [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]the bottle top does not land printed side up[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]the pin does not land point up[[elif test="is(cx=2)"]]a seed does not germinate[[else]]a rider does not wear a helmet[[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]Estimate how many times the bottle top would land printed side up in \({@M@}\) tosses.[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]Estimate how many times the pin would land point up in \({@M@}\) drops.[[elif test="is(cx=2)"]]Estimate how many of \({@M@}\) of these seeds would germinate.[[else]]Estimate how many of \({@M@}\) riders at this junction would wear a helmet.[[/if]]</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[if test="is(cx<2)"]]times[[elif test="is(cx=2)"]]seeds[[else]]riders[[/if]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Relative frequency \(= \dfrac{\text{number of times it happened}}{\text{number of trials}} = \dfrac{{@k@}}{{@N@}} = {@pdec(rf)@}\). This is an estimate of the probability that [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]the bottle top lands printed side up[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]the pin lands point up[[elif test="is(cx=2)"]]a seed germinates[[else]]a rider wears a helmet[[/if]].</p><p>(b) It did not happen in the other \({@N-k@}\) of the \({@N@}\) [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]tosses[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]drops[[elif test="is(cx=2)"]]seeds tested[[else]]riders observed[[/if]], so the estimate is \(1 - {@pdec(rf)@} = {@pdec(ta2)@}\).</p><p>(c) Expected number \(=\) number of trials \(\times\) probability \(= {@M@} \times {@pdec(rf)@} = {@ta3@}\). It is an estimate, not a certainty: the real number will usually be close to this, not exactly equal.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
