  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Probability III: relative frequency and expected frequency</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 3.2: Find a relative frequency as an estimate of a probability, its complement, and an expected number of times.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 5, Section D, questions D2 and D3 of Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP GCSE Mathematics: Foundation 2 for AQA, Edexcel and OCR two-tier GCSE mathematics, Cambridge University Press, 2007: four Kenyan contexts with new data, randomised, with a complement part.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
